  "prompt": "For each month end of 2025, compare LedgerLoop's MRR from subscriptions billed in euros (currency EUR) with the MRR at the end of the same month of 2024. A subscription's MRR on a date is the sum of its subscription_events.mrr_delta_local with event_date on or before that date. fx_rates holds a row for every day of 2024 and 2025, so it can list the month ends. Return four columns, in this order: month_end (the last day of the 2025 month), mrr_eur, mrr_prev_year_eur and growth_pct, the change as a percentage of the 2024 MRR (12.5 for 12.5%), rounded to 1 decimal. Return one row for each month end of 2025. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "month_end",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "mrr_eur",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "mrr_prev_year_eur",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "growth_pct",
